.TH NIX\-SCOUT 1 "August 2026" "nix\-scout 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nix\-scout \- scout module switcher for NixOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nix\-scout
.I command
.RI [ argument ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nix\-scout
materializes, builds, and applies scout modules \(em subflakes under a configured
modules directory.
Each module may export a
.B packages.<system>.scout
output (profile or home\-files facet), a
.B flakelets
output (flakelet daemon facet), or both.
Modules are applied without requiring a full
.BR nixos\-rebuild (8).
.PP
The parent flake\(aqs
.I flake.lock
is stamped into each materialized module so all inputs are pinned consistently.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List available scout modules found under
.IR $NIX_SCOUT_MODULES ,
with facet tags:
.B profile
(bin/ output),
.B home\-files
(home\-files/ output),
.B flakelet
(flakelets.* output).
Each entry is a directory containing a
.IR flake.nix .
.TP
.BI "new " "name [facet\&.\&.\&.]"
Scaffold a new scout module directory under
.IR $NIX_SCOUT_MODULES / name .
Optional
.I facet
arguments are
.BR scout ,
.BR home ,
and
.BR flakelet
(any subset).
Always writes a
.I flake.nix
with the standard facet separation:
.RS
.P
.B lib.optionalAttrs (inputs ? nix\-scout) { # scout # home } // { # flakelet }
.P
Requested facets get stub implementations; omitted facets keep only the denoting comment.
Also writes a placeholder
.I flake.lock
(nixpkgs narHash of zeros; other locked identity fields set to
.BR nix\-scout_not\-real\-lockfile ).
When
.B flakelet
is requested, also writes
.IR settings.nix .
Prints a reminder that a full
.B nixos\-rebuild
is required before any flakelet facet can be registered.
.RE
.TP
.BI switch " name"
Materialize the named module to a temporary directory and apply all present facets:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B package facet
(\c
.IR packages.<system>.scout ):
built via
.BR nix\-build (1)
and applied \(em
.I bin/
installed into the scout profile,
.I home\-files/
copied into
.IR $HOME .
Both sub\-facets are applied when both are present.
.IP \(bu 2
.B flakelet facet
(\c
.IR flakelets.* ):
runs
.B sudo flakelet update <name>
to restart the daemon without a full rebuild.
The flakelet entry must already exist in
.IR /etc/flakelet.json
(populated by
.BR nixos\-rebuild (8)).
If the entry is missing, rebuild once to register it, then retry.
.RE
.TP
.BI switch " path"
Install a store path
.RI ( /nix/store/\&... )
or flake installable
.RI ( ref # attr )
directly into the scout profile without materializing or building a module.
.TP
.B status
Show the active scout profile path, each registered gc\-root, and flakelet service status.
.TP
.B clear
Uninstall all packages from the scout profile, remove gc\-root symlinks, and
delete the Fish
.I conf.d
snippet.
.TP
.B doctor
Check flakelet integration health and print a pass/fail report.
Each check prints
.B [ OK ]
or
.B [FAIL]
with a fix hint. Path\-access failures are mutated in place when
.B doctor
can elevate (same grant as the
.I nix\-scout\-flakelet\-access
activation script):
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B modules\-path access:
verifies the flakelet eval user (read from
.IR /etc/flakelet/config.json ,
field
.B eval_user
or
.BR user ;
defaults to
.IR flakelet )
can reach
.I NIX_SCOUT_MODULES
using
.B primary\-gid\-only
credentials.
Flakelet drops privileges with
.B setuid/setgid
and does
.B not
call
.BR initgroups ,
so supplementary groups such as
.I users
do not help during
.BR "nix flake metadata" .
Fix/mutation: other\-execute on every ancestor directory and other\-rx on the
modules directory and registered module leaves
.RB ( o+x / o+rx ).
.IP \(bu 2
.B state dir:
verifies
.I /var/lib/flakelet
is readable by the current user.
Fix:
.B sudo chgrp flakelet /var/lib/flakelet && sudo chmod g+rx /var/lib/flakelet
or rebuild with the nix\-scout NixOS module (adds the
.I nix\-scout\-flakelet\-access
activation script automatically).
.IP \(bu 2
.B service health:
runs
.B flakelet status \-\-json
and reports any services with a non\-empty
.B last_error
or a
.B held
state.
Skipped if
.I /var/lib/flakelet
is unreadable or
.B flakelet
is not on
.BR PATH .
Fix: repair path access, then
.B sudo flakelet update <name> ;
inspect logs with
.BR "flakelet log <name>" .
.RE
.IP
Exits
.B 1
if any check fails.
.TP
.BI "completions " shell
Print shell completions to stdout.
Supported
.IR shell
values:
.BR fish ,
.BR bash ,
and
.BR zsh .
After
.BR "nix-scout switch" ,
completions ship in the scout profile under
.IR share/fish/vendor_completions.d/nix-scout.fish ,
.IR share/bash-completion/completions/nix-scout ,
and
.IR share/zsh/site-functions/_nix-scout .
Discovery is wired by the shell snippets written on switch (see
.SX FILES ).
.TP
.BR help | \-\-help | \-h
Print usage information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NIX_SCOUT_MODULES
Path to the directory containing scout module subflakes.
Set in
.IR /var/lib/nix-scout/paths
by the nix\-scout NixOS module on activation.
.TP
.B NIX_SCOUT_PARENT
Path to the parent flake root.
Its
.I flake.lock
is copied into each materialized module so inputs are pinned to the same
revisions as the parent.
Set in
.IR /var/lib/nix-scout/paths
by the nix\-scout NixOS module on activation.
.TP
.B NIX_SCOUT_PATHS_FILE
Shell\-sourceable file containing
.BR NIX_SCOUT_PARENT
and
.BR NIX_SCOUT_MODULES
assignments.
Defaults to
.IR /var/lib/nix-scout/paths .
The CLI requires this file; install
.BR inputs.nix-scout.nixosModule
and rebuild if it is missing.
.TP
.B NIX_SCOUT_PROFILE
Full path to the per\-user Nix profile.
Defaults to
.IR /nix/var/nix/profiles/per\-user/$USER/nix\-scout .
.TP
.B NIX_SCOUT_GCROOTS
Full path to the per\-user gc\-roots directory.
Defaults to
.IR /nix/var/nix/gcroots/per\-user/$USER/nix\-scout .
.SH SUDO MODE
.B sudo nix\-scout
is supported.
When run as root,
.B nix\-scout
reads
.B SUDO_USER
and resolves the real invoker\(aqs profile paths and
.B HOME
from
.IR /etc/passwd ,
so all paths remain correct and no secondary
.BR sudo (8)
calls are needed for directory or symlink operations.
Direct invocation as root without
.B SUDO_USER
set is rejected.
.SH SCOUT MODULES
A scout module is a directory under
.I $NIX_SCOUT_MODULES
containing a
.I flake.nix
that may export any combination of:
.IP \(bu 2
.B packages.<system>.scout
\(em a derivation with a
.I bin/
subdirectory (installed into the scout profile via
.BR nix\-env (1))
and/or a
.I home\-files/
subdirectory (each file copied verbatim into
.IR $HOME ).
Both sub\-facets are applied when both are present.
.IP \(bu 2
.B flakelets.<attr>
\(em a Mic92 flakelet service function.
Requires a
.I settings.nix
alongside
.I flake.nix
that returns
.BR "{ enable, output?, settings, autoUpdate? }" .
The nix\-scout NixOS module reads
.I settings.nix
at rebuild time and registers the service into
.B services.flakelets.services
when
.B enable
is true.
.PP
Every scout\-module
.I flake.nix
uses programmatic facet separation so flakelet path evaluation never builds the
scout/home package facet:
.RS
.P
.B lib.optionalAttrs (inputs ? nix\-scout) ( { # scout # home } ) // { # flakelet }
.P
All three section comments are always present; unused sections contain only the comment.
.RE
.PP
Scout modules cannot set system\-wide NixOS options.
Use the core flake or
.B nixos\-rebuild
for that.
.PP
Module
.I flake.nix
outputs receive
.BR systemRebuild :
.B true
when the nix\-scout NixOS module prebuilds all scout modules during a system rebuild
(passed directly into
.IR outputs ).
.B nix\-scout switch
materializes the module and writes
.IR scout\-context.nix
with
.BR systemRebuild = false ;
modules should read it via
.BR nix\-scout.lib.readSystemRebuild
or the same
.IR scout\-context.nix
import pattern.
Use this to ship a lightweight stub during rebuild while installing the full payload
only on explicit switch (e.g. seasonal or space\-heavy tools).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/flakelet/config.json
Flakelet daemon configuration.
.B doctor
reads
.B eval_user
(or
.BR user )
and the registered service names from this file when checking modules\-path access.
.TP
.I /nix/var/nix/profiles/per\-user/$USER/nix\-scout
The dedicated scout Nix profile.
.TP
.I /nix/var/nix/gcroots/per\-user/$USER/nix\-scout/
Directory of gc\-root symlinks preventing installed store paths from being
garbage collected.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fish/conf.d/nix\-scout.fish
Written after a successful profile\-mode install so the scout profile bin is on
.B PATH
and the profile\(aqs
.I share/fish/vendor_completions.d
is prepended to
.BR fish_complete_path ,
.I share
to
.BR XDG_DATA_DIRS ,
and
.I share/man
to
.B MANPATH
(so switch\-installed completions, desktop/mime data, and manpages win over a
stale system copy).
Removed by
.BR "nix\-scout clear" .
Do not edit manually.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bash/nix\-scout.bash
Prepends the scout profile
.I share
to
.BR XDG_DATA_DIRS
(for
.BR bash\-completion (1)
v2) and
.I share/man
to
.B MANPATH .
Sourced automatically when Home Manager
.B programs.bash
is enabled; otherwise add
.B source
to your
.I .bashrc .
Removed by
.BR "nix-scout clear" .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/zsh/nix\-scout.zsh
Prepends
.I share/zsh/site-functions
to
.B fpath
so Zsh loads profile completions via compsys.
Sourced automatically when Home Manager
.B programs.zsh
is enabled; otherwise add
.B source
to your
.I .zshrc .
Removed by
.BR "nix-scout clear" .
.TP
.I Home Manager sessionVariables
When the nix\-scout NixOS module is enabled, Home Manager sets
.BR XDG_DATA_DIRS
and
.B MANPATH
the same way for non\-Fish login sessions (alongside
.BR home.sessionPath
for
.BR PATH ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, module not found, build failure, or one or more
.B doctor
checks failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nix\-env (1),
.BR nix (1),
.BR nixos\-rebuild (8)
